      "text": "Annex 1. Current methodology for WHO",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 25.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        142.64138793945312,
        325.088623046875,
        175.14138793945312
      ],
      "text": "guideline development",
      "font": "SegoeUI",
      "size": 25.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        213.3824005126953,
        527.3905029296875,
        227.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "The formulation of WHO recommendations is based on the Grading of Recommendations Assessment,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.3824005126953,
        527.4223022460938,
        241.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "Development and Evaluation (GRADE) approach. Once evidence has been synthesized through a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        241.3824005126953,
        527.4244384765625,
        255.8253936767578
      ],
      "text": "systematic review approach, evidence reviewers use the GRADE methodology to categorize the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        255.3824005126953,
        527.4373779296875,
        269.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "quality of the evidence into four levels: high, moderate, low or very low (see Table A1.1). The starting",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        269.38238525390625,
        527.4069213867188,
        283.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "point for rating the quality of evidence is always the study design, whereby evidence from RCTs is rated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        283.38238525390625,
        527.41552734375,
        297.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "as high quality, while evidence from non-randomized or observational studies is rated as low quality.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        297.38238525390625,
        527.3892211914062,
        311.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "This value is then adjusted based on additional considerations. Five factors may lower the quality of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        311.38238525390625,
        527.4002685546875,
        325.8254089355469
      ],
      "text": "evidence, namely: limitations in study design and execution, indirectness, imprecision, inconsistency",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        325.3824157714844,
        527.4124755859375,
        339.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "and publication bias. Three factors may increase the quality of evidence from observational studies:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        339.3824157714844,
        449.0429992675781,
        353.825439453125
      ],
      "text": "dose-response gradient, direction of plausible bias and magnitude of the effect  . (1)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        360.4523010253906,
        301.8512268066406,
        375.3203125
      ],
      "text": "Table A1.1 Quality of evidence in GRADE  (1)",
